  "name": "Example: Naming Pyramids",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230697/assets/beed0799de4f42cde58bf0c85f31a1a6850ef1227ea2827e9819a4edeb3ede4a.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?\n\nI. Hexagonal prism\n\nII. Hexagonal pyramid\n\nIII. Rectangular prism",
  "worked_solution": "The solid is a **hexagonal pyramid** since its base is a hexagon and all other $6$ faces meet at a single point\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a hexagonal prism since it doesn't have two identical hexagonal faces connected by equal parallel lines.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles.",
